# Ones and zeros: two Faults, the first hiding the second. A dry Joint on U7 pin 1 (CKB, C4): the leg
# floats high, so the tens' divide-by-5 never counts and the tens are QA alone, 0 or 1. That keeps L6
# low, hiding U11's input C stuck at 0. Once resoldered, the meter is right to 39, then reads the tens
# 4 lower: 47 for 07, 80 % reads 39.
machine knob
title "Ones and zeros"
brief "The left digit only ever shows 0 or 1, whatever the knob does. This one may be a little trickier than it looks."
fault joint U7.1
fault stuck U11.C 0
